      "content": true,
      "reasons": [
        "narrow: The frozen design permits an arm to contain only one group. In that case the displayed within-arm sample variance divides by zero, and the cluster-constant eigenvalue of the residual-maker block is zero, so the ordinary inverse-square-root CR2 adjustment used in the claimed identity is not defined. Requiring at least two groups in each arm is the minimal finite-sample domain condition and is automatic eventually under the paper's treatment-fraction and group-growth assumptions.",
